C2 Target physical pool and Pulsar prepared-record bridge

Date: 2026-10-07
Base: main@abb430a47500871b7e95424e6188886d33830927

DestinationPhysicalAdmission now registers full immutable Target channel generations using their NV20 content keys, sharing the existing Worker/cluster/active/zombie pool and release machinery. Target generations retain their own source-Shard/channel ownership; renewal does not erase old charges. Source-Shard close prevents new/queued sends only for that Shard. Target slots/Profiles/source Shards do not create Lane READY minima; fairness/ordinary protection stays in the existing Target ring/WorkClass graph. Activated registration/slot/Producer/FD counts are still production resource-graph obligations, not authority supplied by this local gate.

PulsarPreparedRecordFactory.targetManaged joins the exact newly PUBLISHING Message and frozen publication with inline or committed-object payload projection, resolved bytes, fixed Journal sequence, full metadata/reserved properties/prepared hash/artifact set. It checks stable producer-name hash against the Target channel and preserves managed timing. This is a pure record join, not a sequence allocator or durable Journal proof. The supplied object Profile/protection and the mapping still require production authorities. Existing record wire schema, Source bodies, tuples, NV values and legacy Lane interfaces are unchanged.

Target bounded submission requires a distinct final ownership hook. Legacy adapter/transport defaults fail closed without invoking the ordinary prepared-record hook. Pinned adapter propagates it into the source-locked P1 transport after builder/value/properties setup and before sendAsync; Source close is checked both after queue wait and at the final hook. The live producer-name hash is checked before SDK construction. Once SEND has been called, synchronous exception or unobservable return propagates to the original bounded zombie fence; it is not converted into an already-completed UNKNOWN physical stage.

